# Build context hygiene. The Unity project is ~1 GB; without this the docker
# daemon tars the whole thing (including regenerable caches) and sends it over the
# socket before the first instruction runs.

# --- Unity regenerable caches (the big ones) ---------------------------------
Library/
Temp/
Obj/
Logs/
UserSettings/
MemoryCaptures/
Recordings/
Build/
Builds/
build/
# NOTE: build/ is excluded from the BUILD image context (Dockerfile.build) but is
# REQUIRED by the runtime image (Dockerfile.worker). Docker uses a single
# .dockerignore per context root, so when building the worker image, run it from a
# context where build/ is present and use the root .dockerignore instead of this
# one — see DEPLOYMENT.md for the exact two-step invocation.

# --- IDE / generated project files -------------------------------------------
*.csproj
*.sln
*.user
*.userprefs
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb
*.mdb

# --- VCS ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- Large artifacts that must never enter a build context -------------------
*.zip
*.7z
*.tar.gz
*.unitypackage
*.sql
*.sql.gz
*.dump

# --- Docs / assets not needed to build ---------------------------------------
docs/
*.md
!distributed/**/*.md
README*
LICENSE*

# --- Python -------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# --- OS -----------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
